{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AuXADu1Z4Q7DHK1YMHEpU7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase-0 Shared Infrastructure â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman handoff)\n2\t\n3\t> SCOPE: this plan is **Phase 0 only** â€” the shared infrastructure every skill cycle reuses. The cognitive\n4\t> skills (Gandalf, Ramanujan, lit-review, data-analysis, ML-code, code-verification), the recreate-a-paper\n5\t> proof, and the NS1 demo are each their OWN researchPrimeâ†’Crucibleâ†’Foreman cycle (see `crucible/PROGRAM-SEQUENCE.md`),\n6\t> NOT waves in this plan. This plan builds the substrate those cycles depend on.\n7\t\n8\t> North Star (program, LOCKED): Build a deep, self-improving skill repository in Skill Foundry where every\n9\t> skill carries a LOCKED North Star, journals its own real-use experience, and is improved during \"sleep\"\n10\t> sessions WITHOUT drifting. First proof (a later cycle): a recreate-a-paper recipe reproducing the Gelman\n11\t> ANOVA paper, graded on architecture/handoff success.\n12\t\n13\tFrozen design: `crucible/MASTER-PLAN.md` (v4). 6 waves, contiguous. Every wave is TAP-gated; the orchestrator\n14\t(not a sub-agent) runs the ground-truth gate after each wave.\n15\t\n16\ttest-command: node --test test/\n17\t\n18\t## EXECUTE/GATE model (FIX-16â€² â€” rest on what Foreman OWNS)\n19\tForeman discards sub-agent transcripts and records no transcript/session id or artifact hash (verified:\n20\tSKILL.md Â§8/Â§10; transport.mjs telemetry). So we do NOT try to prove \"an LLM genuinely ran\" from inside the\n21\tgate. Every deterministic guarantee rests on the two forgery-resistant artifacts the orchestrator OWNS\n22\t(wave-engine.mjs): (a) the **gate artifact** â€” the TAP result of `node --test`, which the ORCHESTRATOR runs;\n23\tand (b) the **post-execute test-file content-hash baseline** (a sub-agent cannot later alter the tests it is\n24\tgraded by). The LLM build work lives in EXECUTE; the deterministic GATE verifies STRUCTURE + runs DETERMINISTIC\n25\ttests. LLM-judge / cross-family judging is ADVISORY (isolated per FIX-15), never part of the gate command\n26\t(PRINCIPLE-D). Build root = this folder (a Node project); templates + canary SETS are written into\n27\t`../../skills/` (Skill Foundry stays stateless prose; canaries are data/refs).\n28\t\n29\t---\n30\t\n31\t## Wave 1 â€” Eval-harness go/no-go spike + test harness bootstrap (P0.A FIX-3/FIX-11/FIX-15)\n32\t**done-when:** `node --test test/` is GREEN and a spike test proves (a) a wrapped validator emits real TAP\n33\t`ok N` events Foreman's gate counts, (b) a PROSE-deliverable coverage path passes the vacuous-green guard\n34\t(an in-root validator/harness file is exercised by an executed test that grades a prose fixture), and (c) an\n35\tUNREACHABLE advisory host leaves the deterministic gate GREEN.\n36\t- **Given** a fresh build root with `package.json` (`scripts.test = node --test test/`), **When** the spike\n37\t  validator grades a fixture prose file and emits TAP, **Then** `node --test` reports â‰¥1 real passing test\n38\t  event and exit 0 (no vacuous-green HALT).\n39\t- **Given** the cross-family advisory host is unreachable (simulated), **When** the wave gate runs, **Then**\n40\t  the gate is GREEN and an advisory \"degraded-coverage\" report artifact is written (failure swallowed; its\n41\t  stdout/exit never reach the gate command).\n42\t- **NO-GO fallback (recorded):** if Foreman-substrate hosting fails the spike, validators run as a standalone\n43\t  Node process Foreman shells to via `test-command` â€” same TAP contract.\n44\t\n45\t## Wave 2 â€” Eval harness: three validators as TAP emitters (P0.A R6/FIX-1/FIX-4/FIX-16â€²)\n46\t**done-when:** one harness exposes three pluggable validators â€” (i) schema+path-existence, (ii) deterministic\n47\tcanary eval, (iii) numeric-tolerance grader (calls a pure offline reference fn) â€” each emitting TAP, with the\n48\tadvisory cross-family judge isolated (FIX-15) so its exit/stdout never reach the gate; `node --test test/` GREEN.\n49\t- **Given** an artifact with a missing referenced path, **When** validator (i) runs, **Then** it emits `not ok`\n50\t  naming the missing path.\n51\t- **Given** a deterministic canary run twice on identical input, **When** validator (ii) runs, **Then** it emits\n52\t  byte-identical TAP both times (no non-determinism in the GATE path).\n53\t- **Given** an unreachable advisory cross-family host, **When** the wave gate runs, **Then** the gate is GREEN\n54\t  and a \"degraded-coverage\" advisory report is written (failure swallowed; FIX-15).\n55\t\n56\t## Wave 3 â€” Machine-checkable handoff-contract gate (P0.B NS5)\n57\t**done-when:** a contract validator gates a stage handoff on schema-valid + all artifact_refs resolve on disk\n58\t+ north_star round-trips byte-identical + open_questions empty; wired so Anchor's HANDOFF.md/NEXT-PROMPT.md and\n59\tCrucible's locate-plan path both emit/validate it; `node --test test/` GREEN.\n60\t- **Given** a handoff doc whose `north_star` differs by one byte from the upstream, **When** the gate runs,\n61\t  **Then** it emits `not ok` (round-trip failure).\n62\t- **Given** a handoff doc with a non-empty `open_questions`, **When** the gate runs, **Then** it emits `not ok`\n63\t  (blocks under-specified handoff).\n64\t\n65\t## Wave 4 â€” Skill-repo templates + tierâ†’model table + swap test (P0.C NS3/NS4/FIX-5)\n66\t**done-when:** the per-skill repo skeleton (NORTH-STAR.md with non-goals as negative tests, SKILL.md,\n67\treferences/, LESSONS.md, journal/, CHANGELOG.md) + the net-new logical-tierâ†’model config table exist; a swap\n68\ttest proves swapping the table changes the resolved model with zero skill-prose edits; `node --test test/` GREEN.\n69\t- **Given** the tierâ†’model table mapping `topâ†’A`, **When** the table is swapped to `topâ†’B` and a persona\n70\t  resolves its model, **Then** the resolved model changes Aâ†’B and no SKILL.md byte changed.\n71\t- **Note:** the swap test pins a model-respecting backend (gemini-cli driver), since the default Claude backend\n72\t  ignores `opts.model` â€” else the test would pass vacuously.\n73\t\n74\t## Wave 5 â€” Journal 7-field schema + North-Star-gated sleep loop (P0.D NS1/NS2/NS3/R5)\n75\t**done-when:** the 7-field journal schema + the sleep meta-recipe (cluster â†’ cross-context-corroborated distill\n76\tâ†’ North-Star gate â†’ eval gate â†’ versioned promote with git rollback) exist and are TAP-tested on FIXTURE\n77\tjournals (real skills do not exist yet); `node --test test/` GREEN.\n78\t- **Given** fixture journal entries where a candidate lesson advances a machine-checkable non-goal, **When** the\n79\t  sleep loop runs, **Then** that lesson is REJECTED (North-Star gate) and logged, not promoted.\n80\t- **Given** a candidate revision that regresses a frozen fixture canary, **When** the eval gate runs, **Then**\n81\t  promotion is blocked and the prior version is retained (rollback).\n82\t- **Given** a candidate lesson corroborated only by same-context repetition, **When** distillation runs, **Then**\n83\t  it is NOT shipped (requires cross-context corroboration, R5).\n84\t\n85\t## Wave 6 â€” Foundry governance wiring + canary versioning + citation hygiene (P0.E/P0.F FIX-6/R7)\n86\t**done-when:** map.json records canary SETS + templates as data/refs (Foundry stays stateless); the drift\n87\tchecker + foundry invariant pytest stay GREEN; canary sets are versioned with skills (append-only; deletion =\n88\thuman call); SkillsBenchâ†’2602.12670 corrected and MemoryGraft dropped in carried docs; `node --test test/` GREEN.\n89\t- **Given** a sleep cycle proposing a canary deletion, **When** governance validates it, **Then** it is BLOCKED\n90\t  as a human-call (append-only enforced).\n91\t- **Given** the Foundry invariant suite, **When** it runs, **Then** it is GREEN (canary/template entries valid,\n92\t  drift checker GREEN).\n93\t\n94\t---\n95\t\n96\t## Project DONE\n97\tDONE = Wave 6 GREEN (orchestrator-run `node --test test/`). At that point the shared substrate exists and is\n98\tproven on fixtures: the deterministic eval harness (3 validators), the machine-checkable handoff contract, the\n99\tper-skill repo templates + swappable tierâ†’model seam, the journal schema + North-Star-gated sleep loop with\n100\trollback, and the Foundry governance wiring. The cognitive-skill cycles, the recreate-a-paper proof, and the\n101\tNS1 demonstration (each its own researchPrimeâ†’Crucibleâ†’Foreman cycle) build ON this substrate next â€” see\n102\t`crucible/PROGRAM-SEQUENCE.md`.\n103\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d1e84d2-4c1b-46ea-87d9-1619b3543ef1","uuid":"91b37c0a-ede8-4586-b6a5-5912c33f5ec6","timestamp":"2026-06-23T00:48:22.152Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\planning\\portfolio-program\\IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md","content":"# Phase-0 Shared Infrastructure â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman handoff)\n\n> SCOPE: this plan is **Phase 0 only** â€” the shared infrastructure every skill cycle reuses. The cognitive\n> skills (Gandalf, Ramanujan, lit-review, data-analysis, ML-code, code-verification), the recreate-a-paper\n> proof, and the NS1 demo are each their OWN researchPrimeâ†’Crucibleâ†’Foreman cycle (see `crucible/PROGRAM-SEQUENCE.md`),\n> NOT waves in this plan. This plan builds the substrate those cycles depend on.\n\n> North Star (program, LOCKED): Build a deep, self-improving skill repository in Skill Foundry where every\n> skill carries a LOCKED North Star, journals its own real-use experience, and is improved during \"sleep\"\n> sessions WITHOUT drifting. First proof (a later cycle): a recreate-a-paper recipe reproducing the Gelman\n> ANOVA paper, graded on architecture/handoff success.\n\nFrozen design: `crucible/MASTER-PLAN.md` (v4). 6 waves, contiguous. Every wave is TAP-gated; the orchestrator\n(not a sub-agent) runs the ground-truth gate after each wave.\n\ntest-command: node --test test/\n\n## EXECUTE/GATE model (FIX-16â€² â€” rest on what Foreman OWNS)\nForeman discards sub-agent transcripts and records no transcript/session id or artifact hash (verified:\nSKILL.md Â§8/Â§10; transport.mjs telemetry). So we do NOT try to prove \"an LLM genuinely ran\" from inside the\ngate. Every deterministic guarantee rests on the two forgery-resistant artifacts the orchestrator OWNS\n(wave-engine.mjs): (a) the **gate artifact** â€” the TAP result of `node --test`, which the ORCHESTRATOR runs;\nand (b) the **post-execute test-file content-hash baseline** (a sub-agent cannot later alter the tests it is\ngraded by). The LLM build work lives in EXECUTE; the deterministic GATE verifies STRUCTURE + runs DETERMINISTIC\ntests. LLM-judge / cross-family judging is ADVISORY (isolated per FIX-15), never part of the gate command\n(PRINCIPLE-D). Build root = this folder (a Node project); templates + canary SETS are written into\n`../../skills/` (Skill Foundry stays stateless prose; canaries are data/refs).\n\n---\n\n## Wave 1 â€” Eval-harness go/no-go spike + test harness bootstrap (P0.A FIX-3/FIX-11/FIX-15)\n**done-when:** `node --test test/` is GREEN and a spike test proves (a) a wrapped validator emits real TAP\n`ok N` events Foreman's gate counts, (b) a PROSE-deliverable coverage path passes the vacuous-green guard\n(an in-root validator/harness file is exercised by an executed test that grades a prose fixture), and (c) an\nUNREACHABLE advisory host leaves the deterministic gate GREEN.\n- **Given** a fresh build root with `package.json` (`scripts.test = node --test test/`), **When** the spike\n  validator grades a fixture prose file and emits TAP, **Then** `node --test` reports â‰¥1 real passing test\n  event and exit 0 (no vacuous-green HALT).\n- **Given** the cross-family advisory host is unreachable (simulated), **When** the wave gate runs, **Then**\n  the gate is GREEN and an advisory \"degraded-coverage\" report artifact is written (failure swallowed; its\n  stdout/exit never reach the gate command).\n- **NO-GO fallback (recorded):** if Foreman-substrate hosting fails the spike, validators run as a standalone\n  Node process Foreman shells to via `test-command` â€” same TAP contract.\n\n## Wave 2 â€” Eval harness: three validators as TAP emitters (P0.A R6/FIX-1/FIX-4/FIX-16â€²)\n**done-when:** one harness exposes three pluggable validators â€” (i) schema+path-existence, (ii) deterministic\ncanary eval, (iii) numeric-tolerance grader (calls a pure offline reference fn) â€” each emitting TAP, with the\nadvisory cross-family judge isolated (FIX-15) so its exit/stdout never reach the gate; `node --test test/` GREEN.\n- **Given** an artifact with a missing referenced path, **When** validator (i) runs, **Then** it emits `not ok`\n  naming the missing path.\n- **Given** a deterministic canary run twice on identical input, **When** validator (ii) runs, **Then** it emits\n  byte-identical TAP both times (no non-determinism in the GATE path).\n- **Given** an unreachable advisory cross-family host, **When** the wave gate runs, **Then** the gate is GREEN\n  and a \"degraded-coverage\" advisory report is written (failure swallowed; FIX-15).\n\n## Wave 3 â€” Machine-checkable handoff-contract gate (P0.B NS5)\n**done-when:** a contract validator gates a stage handoff on schema-valid + all artifact_refs resolve on disk\n+ north_star round-trips byte-identical + open_questions empty; wired so Anchor's HANDOFF.md/NEXT-PROMPT.md and\nCrucible's locate-plan path both emit/validate it; `node --test test/` GREEN.\n- **Given** a handoff doc whose `north_star` differs by one byte from the upstream, **When** the gate runs,\n  **Then** it emits `not ok` (round-trip failure).\n- **Given** a handoff doc with a non-empty `open_questions`, **When** the gate runs, **Then** it emits `not ok`\n  (blocks under-specified handoff).\n\n## Wave 4 â€” Skill-repo templates + tierâ†’model table + swap test (P0.C NS3/NS4/FIX-5)\n**done-when:** the per-skill repo skeleton (NORTH-STAR.md with non-goals as negative tests, SKILL.md,\nreferences/, LESSONS.md, journal/, CHANGELOG.md) + the net-new logical-tierâ†’model config table exist; a swap\ntest proves swapping the table changes the resolved model with zero skill-prose edits; `node --test test/` GREEN.\n- **Given** the tierâ†’model table mapping `topâ†’A`, **When** the table is swapped to `topâ†’B` and a persona\n  resolves its model, **Then** the resolved model changes Aâ†’B and no SKILL.md byte changed.\n- **Note:** the swap test pins a model-respecting backend (gemini-cli driver), since the default Claude backend\n  ignores `opts.model` â€” else the test would pass vacuously.\n\n## Wave 5 â€” Journal 7-field schema + North-Star-gated sleep loop (P0.D NS1/NS2/NS3/R5)\n**done-when:** the 7-field journal schema + the sleep meta-recipe (cluster â†’ cross-context-corroborated distill\nâ†’ North-Star gate â†’ eval gate â†’ versioned promote with git rollback) exist and are TAP-tested on FIXTURE\njournals (real skills do not exist yet); `node --test test/` GREEN.\n- **Given** fixture journal entries where a candidate lesson advances a machine-checkable non-goal, **When** the\n  sleep loop runs, **Then** that lesson is REJECTED (North-Star gate) and logged, not promoted.\n- **Given** a candidate revision that regresses a frozen fixture canary, **When** the eval gate runs, **Then**\n  promotion is blocked and the prior version is retained (rollback).\n- **Given** a candidate lesson corroborated only by same-context repetition, **When** distillation runs, **Then**\n  it is NOT shipped (requires cross-context corroboration, R5).\n\n## Wave 6 â€” Foundry governance wiring + canary versioning + citation hygiene (P0.E/P0.F FIX-6/R7)\n**done-when:** map.json records canary SETS + templates as data/refs (Foundry stays stateless); the drift\nchecker + foundry invariant pytest stay GREEN; canary sets are versioned with skills (append-only; deletion =\nhuman call); SkillsBenchâ†’2602.12670 corrected and MemoryGraft dropped in carried docs; `node --test test/` GREEN.\n- **Given** a sleep cycle proposing a canary deletion, **When** governance validates it, **Then** it is BLOCKED\n  as a human-call (append-only enforced).\n- **Given** the Foundry invariant suite, **When** it runs, **Then** it is GREEN (canary/template entries valid,\n  drift checker GREEN).\n\n---\n\n## Project DONE\nDONE = Wave 6 GREEN (orchestrator-run `node --test test/`). At that point the shared substrate exists and is\nproven on fixtures: the deterministic eval harness (3 validators), the machine-checkable handoff contract, the\nper-skill repo templates + swappable tierâ†’model seam, the journal schema + North-Star-gated sleep loop with\nrollback, and the Foundry governance wiring. The cognitive-skill cycles, the recreate-a-paper proof, and the\nNS1 demonstration (each its own researchPrimeâ†’Crucibleâ†’Foreman cycle) build ON this substrate next â€” see\n`crucible/PROGRAM-SEQUENCE.md`.\n","numLines":103,"startLine":1,"totalLines":103}}}
