{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01NY5hpRuHHaTJZgUWDkFY6x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Skill Foundry â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-runnable): Grounded Summary\n\n**Scope & framing**\n- This plan covers **Phase 0 only** â€” the shared infrastructure every skill cycle reuses; the cognitive skills (Gandalf, Ramanujan, lit-review, data-analysis, ML-code, code-verification), the recreate-a-paper proof, and the NS1 demo are each their *own* researchPrimeâ†’Crucibleâ†’Foreman cycle, not waves here.\n- **Locked program North Star:** build a deep, self-improving skill repository where every skill carries a LOCKED North Star, journals its own real-use experience, and is improved during \"sleep\" sessions *without drifting*; first proof (a later cycle) is a recreate-a-paper recipe reproducing the Gelman ANOVA paper, graded on architecture/handoff success.\n- Frozen design is `crucible/MASTER-PLAN.md` (v4): **6 contiguous waves**, each TAP-gated, with the orchestrator (not a sub-agent) running the ground-truth gate. Test command: `node --test test/`.\n\n**EXECUTE/GATE trust model (FIX-16â€²)**\n- Because Foreman discards sub-agent transcripts and records no session id/artifact hash, the plan does **not** try to prove \"an LLM genuinely ran\" from inside the gate.\n- Every deterministic guarantee rests on two forgery-resistant artifacts the orchestrator owns: (a) the **gate artifact** â€” TAP result of `node --test` run by the orchestrator; and (b) the **post-execute test-file content-hash baseline** (a sub-agent can't later alter the tests it's graded by).\n- LLM build work lives in EXECUTE; the deterministic GATE verifies structure + runs deterministic tests. LLM-judge / cross-family judging is **ADVISORY only** (isolated per FIX-15), never part of the gate command. Skill Foundry stays stateless prose; canaries/templates are written into `../../skills/` as data/refs.\n\n**The six waves (each `done-when` = `node --test test/` GREEN)**\n- **Wave 1 â€” Eval-harness go/no-go spike + test harness bootstrap:** proves a wrapped validator emits real TAP `ok N` events, a prose-deliverable path passes the vacuous-green guard, and an unreachable advisory host still leaves the gate GREEN. NO-GO fallback: validators run as a standalone Node process Foreman shells to via `test-command`.\n- **Wave 2 â€” Three validators as TAP emitters:** one harness exposes (i) schema+path-existence, (ii) deterministic canary eval (byte-identical TAP on repeat), (iii) numeric-tolerance grader calling a pure offline reference fn; advisory cross-family judge isolated so its exit/stdout never reach the gate.\n- **Wave 3 â€” Machine-checkable handoff-contract gate (NS5):** gates a stage handoff on schema-valid + all artifact_refs resolve on disk + north_star round-trips byte-identical + open_questions empty; wired into Anchor's HANDOFF.md/NEXT-PROMPT.md and Crucible's locate-plan path.\n- **Wave 4 â€” Skill-repo templates + tierâ†’model table + swap test (NS3/NS4):** per-skill skeleton (NORTH-STAR.md with non-goals as negative tests, SKILL.md, references/, LESSONS.md, journal/, CHANGELOG.md) + a logical-tierâ†’model config; a swap test proves changing the table changes the resolved model with zero skill-prose edits. Swap test pins a model-respecting backend (gemini-cli driver) since the default Claude backend ignores `opts.model` (else vacuous pass).\n- **Wave 5 â€” Journal 7-field schema + North-Star-gated sleep loop (NS1/NS2):** the sleep meta-recipe (cluster â†’ cross-context-corroborated distill â†’ North-Star gate â†’ eval gate â†’ versioned promote with git rollback), TAP-tested on **fixture** journals (real skills don't exist yet). Lessons advancing a non-goal are rejected; canary-regressing revisions are blocked (rollback); same-context-only corroboration is not shipped (R5).\n- **Wave 6 â€” Foundry governance wiring + canary versioning + citation hygiene (FIX-6/R7):** map.json records canary SETS + templates as data/refs; drift checker + foundry invariant pytest stay GREEN; canary sets are versioned append-only (deletion = human call); SkillsBenchâ†’2602.12670 corrected and MemoryGraft dropped in carried docs.\n\n**Definition of done**\n- **Project DONE = Wave 6 GREEN** (orchestrator-run `node --test test/`): the shared substrate exists and is proven on fixtures â€” the 3-validator eval harness, the machine-checkable handoff contract, the per-skill repo templates + swappable tierâ†’model seam, the journal schema + North-Star-gated sleep loop with rollback, and the Foundry governance wiring.\n- The cognitive-skill cycles, the recreate-a-paper proof, and the NS1 demonstration build *on* this substrate next, each as its own researchPrimeâ†’Crucibleâ†’Foreman cycle (per `crucible/PROGRAM-SEQUENCE.md`).\n\n---\nOne note on grounding: you referred to a planning *trio* session with multiple member documents, but only one document (this Implementation Plan) was named. The summary above is grounded entirely in `planning/portfolio-program/IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md`. If you want me to fold in the companion docs (`crucible/MASTER-PLAN.md`, `PROGRAM-SEQUENCE.md`, the phase-0 research `FINDINGS.md`/`DELIVERABLE.md`), say the word and I'll cross-reference them."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":638,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3549,"cache_read_input_tokens":30359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3549},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d1e84d2-4c1b-46ea-87d9-1619b3543ef1","uuid":"ab3cfabd-016c-4f1d-a0e9-e987b2d8721c","request_id":"req_011CcKGgTsdZSqiqme4wR3sC"}
